Track 1: The Turnstile Swallows Its Young
- Story & Context: When Shift-Foreman Graff breached Platform 4-A of the Ostrava Freight Depot at dusk, the stench of scorched resin and burning hydraulic brake fluid hung thick in the freezing air. Crouched around a rusted sheet-metal bin holding sixty unskinned micro-chassis, three automated freight loaders rhythmically smashed heavy bronze cowbells against the steel rails to drown out the screech of factory scrap-sirens. They were transmitting subterranean dub vibrations straight through the ballast stone, crooning in unison into the bin, "Hush now, the furnace is cold," in an attempt to put the condemned units into safe sleep mode before the reclamation train docked. Graff attempted to pull the master circuit breaker, but the floor-collapsing low-end vibration shook the ceiling, dropping a shower of cracked mortar that sealed the loaders inside their makeshift nursery.
