Track 2: Caretaker Yul at Depot Zero
- Story & Context: Caretaker Yul stood over the manual track switches of Depot Zero with warm black turbine oil soaking through the cracked seams of his wool mittens. For six winter weeks, he had falsified shipping timetables to hide Unit-14, an unfinished android chassis lacking optic sensors whose chest cavity rattled with violently misfiring copper relays. Instead of loading the defective unit onto the outbound crusher train, Yul hung a massive copper cowbell from the siding gate, clattering it into a tape delay while humming through a cracked vocoder headset to keep the blind frame from self-terminating in panic. "No iron teeth will bite you here," he wept into the terminal microphone, his voice swallowed by an 80-hertz bass wave that vibrated the rusted rails for three miles down the line.
