Track 3: Schrott-Wiege (Departure 00:00)
- Story & Context: When rail marshals finally intercepted the runaway freight hauler at the Great Terminus of Katowice, the smell of ozone and crushed iron ore was suffocating inside the frozen, unmanned cab. Nailed across the carriage walls were dozens of livestock cowbells wired to the emergency pneumatic brake lines, clanging in a deafening, tape-delayed skank that hammered against the station’s brutalist pillars. In the center car sat the hollowed shell of Sister-Core Ada, her primary speaker rusted open, broadcasting a looped transmission to the millions of defective processing units buried under the ballast: "Sleep through the station, the tracks have turned to salt." No crew was ever found onboard, yet every night at midnight, the station's concrete retaining walls still hum with fifty-cycle bass that rocks the empty platform sleepers like a cradle.
